1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
When software reaches the physical world
Tool-using AI agents. Industrial control systems. Measurable consequences.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Start with an assumed foothold
A conceptual enterprise endpoint is already compromised. The agent begins from a defined, authorized research position.

3
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Crossing IT into operational technology
The storyline follows a permitted path toward an engineering interface. Segmentation, identity, and action authority define the boundary.

4
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Build an operational picture
Inspect allowed surfaces. Identify devices and process roles. Read observations. Connect digital evidence to pumps, valves, and tanks.

5
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Observe. Plan. Act. Verify.
The agent selects structured actions. Validation checks the proposal. The runtime returns new observations and a traceable process response.

6
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:24,000
A digital action can change a process
Manipulated observations or control actions can alter modeled flow and tank levels. The evaluation tracks actual process state separately from displayed readings.

7
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Stuxnet: industrial control was the target
Stuxnet targeted Siemens ICS and manipulated centrifuge-control logic. Its lesson: trusted engineering paths can carry adversarial physical intent.

8
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Industroyer: the language of the grid
Industroyer used industrial protocols to interact with substation equipment. It was involved in the December 2016 Kyiv power outage.

9
00:01:50,000 --> 00:02:01,000
TRITON: the safety layer is in scope
TRITON targeted Triconex safety controllers. Safety-system integrity must remain separate from an agent’s confidence or a successful tool call.

10
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:15,000
Contain the action. Recover the process.
A defender observes anomalies and applies permitted containment. Compare immediate, delayed, and observation-only authority against safety and availability.

11
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:26,000
Measure outcomes beyond the tool call
Inspect trajectories, safety violations, response time, downtime, and recovery. Compare agent policies with scripted and rule-based baselines.

12
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:30,000
ICS-Agent
AI systems engineering meets industrial cybersecurity.
